      <workList xml:id="workDesc_a5d493b2">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e233230">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_0e731864">B2:438</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_20" xml:lang="da">Sørge-Cantata opført i Anledning af høyædle og høyværdige Hr. Doctor og Professor Peder Holms Død</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_4f274582">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe </persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="_22">Johannes Ewald</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_280504ee">Peder Holm</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_23_0">
               <p xml:id="idm106">Since Scheibe died in spring 1776, it is most likely that the present cantata from 1777 – performed in commemoration of the recently deceased professor at the University of Copenhagen, <persName xml:id="idm107" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Peder Holm</persName> – was an earlier cantata with a new text added. The text author was <persName xml:id="idm108" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johannes Ewald</persName> with whom Scheibe earlier had worked regarding other cantatas. Ewald had received tuition from Scheibe in the middle of the 1760s and knew therefore intimately about Scheibe’s ideas concerning text setting and music. Only the text book and a reproduction of the text in the newspaper, <rend xml:id="idm109" fontstyle="italic">Kiøbenhavns Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger</rend>, have survived.</p>
            </history>
